      <div class="section-head">The Delagar Dynasty — 0 to 358 AC</div>

      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">0 AC</span>
        <p>Rhaegon Delagar crowned. The five realms formally dissolved and reorganized as regions of a single kingdom. The Faith of the Two established — Radum and Iddia. The Common Tongue mandated. Ashfort founded as the capital.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">89 AC</span>
        <p>House Mévouimeur first appears in the historical record, a family of builders commissioned for public structures in Arset's capital. Their work consistently exceeds the brief. The family's three-century rise to cultural and political dominance begins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">c. 285 AC</span>
        <p>Hirum Mévouimeur born. Amara Ravenscroft born — his future wife and mother of James.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">288 AC</span>
        <p>The Crown Prince of Avelyn is born — Eleanor's older brother, first child of the reigning king.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">289 AC</span>
        <p>Princess Eleanor born in Avelyn, second child and first daughter of the reigning king. She and her brother are close from childhood, one year apart, temperamentally similar, genuinely fond of each other.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">c. 300 AC</span>
        <p>James Mévouimeur born, son of Hirum. Carries Mévouimeur blood through his father, Ravenscroft blood through his mother Amara, and Vero blood through his grandmother Sarah.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">307 AC</span>
        <p>Eleanor, aged eighteen, falls in love with a Northern lord on a trade delegation. She runs off and marries Henrik Vassennes. Eleanor arrives in the North and begins building a new life. Hirum Mévouimeur courts and marries Amara Ravenscroft.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">309 AC</span>
        <p>Eleanor, age twenty, gives birth to her first child Charles.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">c. 310 AC</span>
        <p>Hirum Mévouimeur dies. James inherits the estate and the Mévouimeur name.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">315 AC</span>
        <p>Eleanor gives birth to her second and last child Charlotte. The same year, the Crown Prince of Avelyn dies at twenty-seven. The future king, sixteen years old, becomes heir overnight. Eleanor loses her closest sibling and last real connection to a court that might have welcomed her home. It breaks something in her that never fully heals.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">330 AC</span>
        <p>Jacob Mévouimeur dies at eighteen — a casualty of one of Hirum's political gambits gone irreparably wrong. James is sixteen when he watches it happen.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">331 AC</span>
        <p>Eleanor dies at age forty-two. Charlotte is sixteen, Charles is twenty-two. The Northern lord dies the same year, leaving Charles fully in charge. Charlotte is devastated — Eleanor was the one person who made the house feel livable.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">333 AC</span>
        <p>Charlotte, eighteen, is married to Lord James by Charles, who is drowning in debt. James is charming in company and cold behind closed doors. The mask slips within months. Henry is born the same year. Charlotte loves him ferociously from the first moment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">333–346 AC</span>
        <p>Charlotte endures thirteen years of James's cruelty — abuse, public humiliation, systematic isolation. Letters are monitored; visits are discouraged and eventually refused. Charlotte has no one except Henry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">346 AC</span>
        <p>Charlotte takes her own life at age thirty-one. Henry is thirteen years old.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">c. 359–360 AC</span>
        <p>Charles Vassennes dies at approximately fifty years old. The cause recorded was illness. The cause understood by everyone who knew him was simpler and worse: he had run out of reasons to continue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">358 AC</span>
        <p>Willow Mévouimeur is born.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">364 AC</span>
        <p>Beatrice Mévouimeur disappears. Willow is six years old. The weeks surrounding Beatrice's disappearance do something thorough to Willow's memory. Henry unravels. In the same year, Willow is brought to court and introduced to Prince Arlan and his twin sister Alisanne, aged eight. Henry agrees that Willow will be presented as a potential match for Arlan when both come of age — in exchange for keeping the Vassennes lands.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">c. 365–366 AC</span>
        <p>Isabelle Vassennes, age sixteen, disappears. Presumed dead, never confirmed. House Vassennes is formally dissolved. Its lands and debts pass to House Mévouimeur.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">378 AC</span>
        <p>James Mévouimeur dies at sixty-eight.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">379 AC</span>
        <p>Aldric Ravenscroft killed during the early stages of the Killana Rebellion. Cressida Vero dies, most likely of the Silent Death. Marick Ravenscroft and Kenna Vero each inherit their houses at age 23 and 21 respectively.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-entry">
        <span class="timeline-year">381 AC</span>
        <p>Henry Mévouimeur dies at forty-eight. Lady Willow is twenty-three. The chronicle's present year.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

